# Nautomation Prime Cisco Discovery Audit - optional environment variables
#
# NOTE: the application does NOT read a .env file. These are ordinary
# environment variables; set them in your shell, or as user/system variables
# in Windows, before launching. This file exists only to document them.
#
# Device credentials are never configured here. They come from the Windows
# Credential Manager, or from the prompts on the setup screen, so that no
# plaintext password is ever written to disk.
#
# ── Windows Credential Manager targets (optional overrides) ──────────────────
# CDP_PRIMARY_CRED_TARGET=MyApp/ADM
# CDP_ANSWER_CRED_TARGET=MyApp/ANSWER
#
# ── Discovery scope and connection (optional overrides) ──────────────────────
# CDP_JUMP_SERVER=bastion.example.com
# CDP_LIMIT=10
#
# ── Diagnostics (optional) ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Alternate logging configuration file.
# LOGGING_CONFIG=C:\path\to\logging.conf
#
# Write the full raw CDP/LLDP command output to logs/debug.log. This is a
# complete topology dump - neighbour names, management IPs, platforms and
# software versions - so it is off by default. Enable only while
# troubleshooting parsing, and treat the resulting log as sensitive.
# CDP_DEBUG_RAW=1
